                <pb facs="0745" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4909: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-29T16:00:00+08:00">March 29, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 29—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Situation reports numbers 13 to 17 were not telegraphed being of no special
                    importance.</p>
                <p>Following is situation report number 18, March 29: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <list>
                            <item>“[1.] Numerous reports from neutral observers along Chinese front
                                confirm impression that incidents are occurring between the two
                                sides more especially in the region of Taitsang. A recent incident
                                puts beyond reasonable doubt that a strong Japanese patrol made an
                                attack on a small Chinese escort accompanying a neutral observer in
                                vicinity of Wunglichiao near Taitsang.</item>
                            <item>2. Japanese aerial reconnaissances are now intensified over
                                Chinese line.</item>
                            <item>3. Japanese staff have today issued orders with a view to prevent
                                recurrence of incidents reported in paragraph 1, above.”</item>
                        </list></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
